# What `docker build .` must not send to the daemon.
#
# The build context is the repository root, and this is a denylist of the large
# git-ignored trees rather than an allowlist of what the images COPY. An
# allowlist would have to be revised every time a `COPY` in docker/*.dockerfile
# does; this list only has to name things that are big and that nothing copies.
#
# CI builds from a fresh checkout, where none of these exist -- which is why
# their absence went unnoticed. Locally `build/` alone is gigabytes, and every
# `docker build` was sending it.
#
# Keep in step with .gitignore: anything added there that is large belongs here
# too. The reverse does not hold -- .gitignore also hides small files that cost
# nothing to send.

# The staged build trees; see "Working on mpif" in CLAUDE.md
build*/

# doc/mpi50-report.pdf and friends: tens of megabytes, read by dev/ tooling only
doc/

# The generator's input. gen/ is generated *and committed*, so the images build
# from gen/ and never run dev/mpiapi.jl
data/

# Nothing here reads the repository's history: no CMakeLists.txt or ci-scripts
# script runs git against the context, and install-mpich.sh clones over the
# network
.git/

*~
.DS_Store
